  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nIn sense 2, {導|みちび}く is often combined with {出|だ}す to form {導|みちび}き{出|だ}す (to derive, to work out), which is very common in academic and scientific contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {勝利|しょうり}に{導|みちび}く — to lead to victory\n- {成功|せいこう}に{導|みちび}く — to guide to success\n- {結論|けつろん}を{導|みちび}き{出|だ}す — to derive a conclusion\n- {答|こた}えを{導|みちび}く — to arrive at an answer\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{案内|あんない}する is to guide in the sense of showing around or giving directions. {率|ひき}いる means to lead or command a group. {導|みちび}く emphasizes guiding toward a positive outcome or correct answer.",
